{"title":"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> denote the sum of all positive factors of an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Find the value of the sum of all natural numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eeb377f6ff79e5147160fb99c7a0e45abfc15a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\le 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is odd.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want to find the sum of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/5/fa58d86cf2e6fe5608057db9bbb05bfbb3f86e51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\le225, n\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" /> such that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/1/3f1057225f12fcf8268bdecc2aead7f54c3716fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S(n) = \\sum_{d\\mid n}d \\equiv 1 \\pmod{2}\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"41\" />\nNotice that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08e0e448e48d232d0ae72d3d3247a55354a3ba29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=p_1^{e_1}p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"19\" />, if we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/4/ba4cb246e4c5003851dd0e1eaa8ab650474b1594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, then:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123138a5cd220f1afaac93ec5001b9f4c77f3e09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S(n)=S(2^{e_1}p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r})=(1+2^1+\\dots+2^{e_1})S(p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r})\\]\" width=\"455\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b82a4dd318ed13fa1aa90d1cbb76aa0fccdf43c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S(n)=S(p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r}) + 2\\cdot S(p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r}) + 2^2\\cdot S(p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r}) + \\dots + 2^{e_1}\\cdot S(p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r})\\]\" width=\"598\" height=\"20\" />\n(For example, we can rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abfb0229fe2b032486bc524afa36cc7d37c982b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34da996e625e768eeb9b36696696970d3d96a960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(12)=2(1+3)+4(1+3)+(1+3)=1+2+3+4+6+12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"496\" height=\"20\" />)\n</p><p>Taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/8/ed8862df397b4abfdeecf2ac70d247e39b160995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e344d0fd0b93a20fb4bbcec89699b4eccf642da1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S(n)\\equiv S(p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r}) + (0)\\cdot S(p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r}) + \\dots (0)\\cdot S(p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r}) \\equiv S(p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r}) \\pmod{2}\\]\" width=\"672\" height=\"18\" />\nNow, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1126d5c39eff72637ff64aa9dc012c676fb679.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_2,p_3\\dots p_r\\neq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />, our goal is to find all odd integers such that the sum of their positive divisors is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b7d281e8bbf8e1be8d86d66083f032193e57e71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\bmod 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />. Notice that since every odd integer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35a5d2bc369085de642e727e5f4afd40c3043c4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\bmod 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, then the divisors of an odd integer must also be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b7d281e8bbf8e1be8d86d66083f032193e57e71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\bmod 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be an odd integer, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14026b461e5c8f1ac2f1dfa61b92f9179353a1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> denote the number of divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Then:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfedf2474aad3fb76817cf247cbfb6500fb812c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S(k)\\equiv\\sum_{d\\mid k} d \\equiv \\underbrace{1 + 1 + 1 \\dots + 1}_{\\tau(k) \\text{ times}} \\pmod{2}\\]\" width=\"330\" height=\"44\" />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74b9d8caa32e164594e695c19fece20f45b8c6b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b7d281e8bbf8e1be8d86d66083f032193e57e71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\bmod 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, then the amount of divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14026b461e5c8f1ac2f1dfa61b92f9179353a1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b7d281e8bbf8e1be8d86d66083f032193e57e71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\bmod 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />. Notice that only perfect squares fit this requirement, since if one of the prime exponents is odd, then that would mean <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14026b461e5c8f1ac2f1dfa61b92f9179353a1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> is even.  (Also note that:)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5dc568b394894c5d08133e163e8020f7e56ee31.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tau(k)=\\tau(p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_r^{e_r})=\\prod_{i=2}^r (e_i+1)\\]\" width=\"260\" height=\"47\" />\nSo, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> to have the property <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/2/1e22fdd317cb950779a7c63e5ce0191be7ce5f46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(k)\\equiv 1 \\pmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> must be a perfect square. Since we want to find the sum of all possible values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that also have this property, we can use our definition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/69713319059c1236c4025e30660b3a2f47927007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2^{e_1}k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />. Regardless of what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f814fcbba7b623f656f7ce45b87262a9cf562dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is (as long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2740f0d5ee7e51b529d67d4821f8de53adeafc08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le e_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c451ec8f773e073b9c486b3dd76bdd4bd59fc286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\le225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />), as long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is an odd perfect square, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is valid. Divide into cases for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f814fcbba7b623f656f7ce45b87262a9cf562dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/1/f61bc914d7419b8cd20797ddbb574c3c50b4b46f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />:</b> Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/1/64171298bed4ce3bf5dccfae0b958ab2ee5259c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\{1,9,25,49,81,121,169,225\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"264\" height=\"20\" /></li>\n<li><b>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d4087722363c8f5879bee0e7ae3119479e826e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />:</b> Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea7ee8a282949fd853a01537ec7a2b55e56f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55d9b34a442d4131be97f897fc5203ec4441315e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\{2,18,50,98,162\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" /></li>\n<li><b>Case 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de19f23c4273e8db31b52af6dd124e277aa3dbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />:</b> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e758eaa0f61ac21dadc9767937e054b92674004f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\{4,36,100,196\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" /></li>\n<li><b>Case 4: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/2/f22e60ca5d9b00e1d07cb253fe5110cb1c8ec4bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12dfee9bd48621059ece6520d38c255cf08d4fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\{8,72,200\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /></li>\n<li><b>Case 5: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf429d59822ecd7372abc91826142dec643fe07c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd4c6fd6423352aa115cdd84e06e78dbf917e423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\{16, 144\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" /></li>\n<li><b>Case 6: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a7bd6b4475e12da3c6bc44704bbfdcbea6335a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1=5,6,7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />:</b> (These fit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c451ec8f773e073b9c486b3dd76bdd4bd59fc286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\le225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> only at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, otherwise they would be outside the bounds): <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0c48eabc34fbb70c3e6354cd77b2883a3501f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\{32,64,128\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Now, we only need to sum all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0cebd683db3b017ce03e827630d6331b32c01db7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{S(n)\\bmod 2 \\equiv 1} n = \\boxed{2010}\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"42\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO\">2026 Indonesia District MO </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">20</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indonesia_District_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Indonesia District MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Indonesia District MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018034945\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 260/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2040/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10988/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.135      1 Template:Indonesia_District_MO_box\n100.00%    8.135      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37857:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018034945 and revision id 292508. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}